<title>BELGIUM: EU expected to make Boeing announcement 1000 GMT.</title>
<headline>EU expected to make Boeing announcement 1000 GMT.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission was in discussions on Monday on whether to approve the Boeing / McDonnell Douglas merger and an announcement was expected to be made at around 1000 GMT, EU sources said.</p>
<p>European Union Competition Commissioner Karel Van Miert is due to hold a press conference on the issue at that time.</p>
<p>EU sources earlier said that the Commission looked set to give its blessing in principle to the planned $15 billion plane manufacturing merger. But a formal decision by the European Union's 20-seat executive, planned for today, was expected to be delayed for several days.</p>
<p>Boeing has scheduled a separate press conference for 1130 GMT.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom +32 2 287 68 11</p>
